                <head>253. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On January 2, 1959, General Lauris
                    Norstad, Supreme Allied Commander, Europe, informed the military
                    representatives of the Greek and Turkish Governments at NATO Headquarters in Paris that he was ready to initiate formal
                    discussions regarding the deployment of IRBMs in Greece and Turkey. For
                    documentation on the U.S. decision to place intermediate range ballistic
                    missiles in Greece and Turkey, see <ref target="#d331">Documents 331</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </div>
